The whole set at once: kinds, overtime, gear, waves and regulars, played together.
Everything below is the output of tools/sim, kept as printed. PART 1 is the final pass; read that first.

Final constants, all in src/game/rules.ts:
  SERVE_PATIENCE_FLOOR_MS 25 s   MOVED HERE, from 30 s. The only constant this pass moved.
  Everything else stands as mechanics-stage3.out left it:
  ORDER_PATIENCE_FLOOR_MS 12 s, DAY_PATIENCE_FLOOR_MS 65 s, FIRST_WAVE 3, MAX_WAVE 6, WAVE_GROWTH_DAYS 5,
  LULL 6-10 s, WAVE_GAP 1.2-2.2 s, LINE_MS 35 s, BENCH_LINE_PATIENCE 1.5, OVERTIME_PATIENCE 0.7,
  OVERTIME_BONUS_PER_ROUND 0.1, OVERTIME_BURN_KEEPS 0.5, OVERTIME_MAX_ROUNDS 3, REGULAR_AT 0.6 then 0.2,
  USUAL_MAX_TILES 4, STREAK_CAP 5, gear prices 200/400/800/1500, and all the kind rules.

Which part was run on what:
  PART 1  node tools/sim/run5.cjs 300, the final constants. Every cell is a morning a chained shop has reached.
  PART 2  the build before any of this: a copy of 67ae6fd, on the same seeds. Its bot had no noticeMs, so the
          habit rows ran with that one line added. Day 2 and the three-star days of 30 are from here too:
          baseline/run.out has neither.
  PART 3  the sweeps that chose the floor: n=300 fine, then n=150 coarse. Rows ran on the floor they name.
  PART 4  sections A, B and I of the same pass on the floor as it stood, 30 s, so the move can be read off.

Only the human is modelled, and the timing is assumed. No real drink has been timed. See section J.


################ PART 1. FINAL PASS, n=300

=== A. EVERYTHING ON, AGAINST THE BASELINE: kinds, waves, regulars, gear, overtime; upright; n=300 per cell ===
Each cell is the morning a chained shop has reached. money includes whatever the jar paid. never/calm/always are overtime policies; calm presses only with nobody outside and at most two others on the counter, hearts above half.
base = baseline/run.out as printed, day 12 from its day 14 row, day 2 run off a copy of 67ae6fd.
